DESCRIPTION:Event by TAG'S SUMMER STAGE\n3037 State Route 352\, Big Flats
 \, NY\nPublic\nMulti-platinum superstar Russell Dickerson is bringing his 
 incredible live show to the Mich Ultra Summer Stage at Tag’s in Big Flat
 s\, NY on Friday\, August 21\, with special guest Niko Moon. It’s a can
 ’t-miss night summer night in the Southern Tier.\nTickets available for 
 purchase online at tagstickets.com\, by phone 800-650-TAGS\, or in person 
 at Tag’s Restaurant\nTickets – INCLUDES ALL FEES: *\nGeneral Admission
 : $52.39\nReserved Seating: $64.39 - $100.39\nGold Circle: $112.39 - $148.
 39\n*10% Off Early Bird Pricing in effect on all tickets up until two week
 s out from the show. Tickets will revert to regular price 08/06/2026 at mi
 dnight.\nAdd-Ons (do not include price of ticket):\nVENUE VIP Experience: 
 $125.00\nVIP Parking: $40.00\nEarly Entry: $25.00\nExpress Lane: $20.00\nR
 ussell Dickerson: Multi-Platinum chart-topper and Triple Tigers entertaine
 r Russell Dickerson is no stranger to the grind. The country headliner fir
 st broke through by wearing his heart on his sleeve\, launching a string o
 f five deeply romantic No. 1 hits: “Yours” (3X Platinum)\, “Blue Tac
 oma” (2X Platinum)\, “Love You Like I Used To” (2X Platinum)\, “Ev
 ery Little Thing”(Platinum)\, and “God Gave Me a Girl.” He followed 
 that success with the slinky\, soul-infused “She Likes It” (with Jake 
 Scott) (2X Platinum)\, further showcasing his genre-blending style. Often 
 inspired by his happy home life\, they powered a rise which now includes 3
  billion career streams\, industry-wide accolades and a solid reputation f
 or lyrical brilliance\, rooted in feel-good reflection and paired a good-n
 atured grin. But what fans of his singles couldn’t always see was Dicker
 son’s fiery\, sold-out tour showmanship. That changed with his highly an
 ticipated fourth studio album\, FAMOUS BACK HOME. Blending the tender fami
 ly man with the wild-eyed performer from his SOLD-OUT RUSSELLMANIA TOUR 20
 25\, the project marked a new era of confidence and creative range. Leadin
 g with the dance-floor-ready single “Happen to Me\,” a seize-the-momen
 t rocker full of sonic swagger\, landed on the Billboard Hot 100 and score
 d his biggest streaming debut week yet. FAMOUS BACK HOME delivers a bold b
 lend of country-soul\, ‘80s rock\, and modern pop pushing sonic boundari
 es while keeping Dickerson’s signature heart-on-sleeve sincerity. It’s
  his most personal and dynamic project yet. Adding to the excitement\, Dic
 kerson is releasing a brand-new four-song EP on March 6\, giving fans fres
 h music just as tickets go on sale. The new project showcases the next cha
 pter of his high-energy\, hook-driven sound and is expected to bring even 
 more momentum to his 2026 tour run. For more\, visit RussellDickerson.com
 \nNiko Moon: When Niko Moon first emerged with his triple-platinum smash 
 “GOOD TIME\,” the Texas-born singer/songwriter lit up the country scen
 e with his larger-than-life energy and heartfelt message of radical positi
 vity. On his latest LP AMERICAN PALM\, the Nashville-based that mission to
  a whole new level and immerses the audience in the idyllic landscape that
  never fails to lift his spirits: the sun-soaked serenity and mind-blowing
  splendor of the beach. A top-notch lyricist who got his start as a co-wri
 ter for the Zac Brown Band and later penned hits for superstars like Morga
 n Wallen and Rascal Flatts\, Niko matches his feel-good fusion of country 
 and timeless pop with plenty of colorful storytelling\, instantly submergi
 ng the senses in the blissed-out surroundings of the coast. Made with prod
 ucer Danny Majic (an L.A.-based producer/songwriter who’s worked with On
 eRepublic\, Flo Rida\, Galantis\, and more)\, the result is a seaside geta
 way in the form of an album—equal parts carefree\, contemplative\, and w
 ildly life-affirming .Whether he’s delivering a summer-ready anthem like
  “BOAT SONG” or a gently swaying country tune like “KING OF THE ISLA
 ND” (a duet with his father\, Cris Cowan)\, Niko imbues every song on AM
 ERICAN PALM with the deep intentionality he’s embraced since “GOOD TIM
 E” (No. 1 single that served as the title track to his Billboard 200-cha
 rting 2021 debut album).Through the years Niko’s sense of purpose has on
 ly gotten stronger\, leading him to launch the Happy Cowboy Foundation(a n
 onprofit that supports mental-health initiatives and addiction-recovery pr
 ograms) and Happy Himalayan (a premium artesian water brand infused with p
 ink Himalayan sea salt).As his reach continues to expand exponentially\, N
 iko looks forward to taking AMERICAN PALM on the road and interacting up-c
 lose with his vast community of fans.“ Very few things can unite thousan
 ds and thousands of people from all walks of life\, but music can\,” he 
 says. “It’s an incredibly powerful energy\, and as artists we’re abl
 e to utilize it for good or for bad. My goal is always to harness that ene
 rgy to take people in a positive direction\, and create an experience wher
 e we can all gather and connect and celebrate life together.”\n\nSource:
  FLXcalendar - https://calendar.time.ly/o9b0uzpj/event/78403125/2026082118
