DESCRIPTION:Event by Gourdlandia and Ithaca Children's Garden\nIthaca Chil
 dren's Garden\n592 Taughannock Blvd\nIthaca\, NY\nDuration: 2 hr 30 min\nP
 ublic\nCreate a gourd snout\, and strut about! Partake of exotic snacks\, 
 enjoy the music\, learn a bit\, and generally have a very gourd time. In t
 he end\, the new picture book from Gourdlandia\, Vivalina Grows A Gourd\, 
 will be launched in style.\nOpen a gourd! Scrape it\, color it\, drill hol
 es (nostrils!)\, add a string. This is a party for makers\, young and old.
  Music by The Human Sprockets: Sam Schmidt\, Richie Stearns\, Joe Hayward 
 and Pete Thompson. Samosas\, spring rolls\, and other delicious treats by 
 the local Karen-Burmese community (donations will support a school in a re
 mote Burmese village). A few words\, a song or two\, and the gourds will b
 e thoroughly extolled!\nIf you enjoy gourds on parade\, you will certainly
  enjoy Vivalina's Gourd-a-Palooza\, with or without a youngster in tow.\n
 \nSource: FLXcalendar - https://calendar.time.ly/o9b0uzpj/event/78441679/2
